# UI and Design System

## Design documentation

- Any UI work must refer to `/docs/design` documentation before implementing.
- If design guidance is missing for the requested UI, stop and ask the user rather than inventing a new visual system.

## Design tokens

- Use design tokens instead of direct CSS value definitions (raw colors, spacing, font sizes, radii, shadows, etc.).
- Prefer token references from the design system (CSS variables, theme tokens, or documented token names in `docs/design`).
- Do not introduce one-off hardcoded visual values when a token exists or should be added via design docs.

Examples:

- Prefer: `color: var(--color-text-primary);` or the project's token API
- Avoid: `color: #1a1a1a;` unless the design docs explicitly require a one-off and the user approves it

## New components

- Do not create new UI components without explicit user approval.
- Prefer composing or extending existing components.
- If a new component seems necessary, propose it (name, responsibility, API sketch) and wait for approval before adding files.
